proxy reads, in co_localsplusnames' order (tbobj.go's frameSlots; queue 219)"] [55 2 "// lineStarts are the instructions that may start a line event, by instruction (trace.go's traceLines; queue 219t)"] [57 2 "// monLocal are the code's local sys.monitoring events by tool (set_local_events, monitoring.go; queue 281), nil for none"] [59 2 "// obj is the code's object (co_* attributes), one per code so that frame.f_code is func.__code__ (queue 219t)"] [61 2 "// top is the code's facts its nested codes ask of their outermost code (queue 229's parent, py-small-1127): the code"] [62 2 "// whose constant this is reached by top.up, never by a pointer to the Code itself (a nested code holding its parent"] [63 2 "// held the parent's constants, its own code object among them: a function's code was never collected)"] [65 2 "// view is CPython's bytecode of the code, made when asked (bytecode_asm.go)"] [67 26 "// the jumps flow! threaded (the IR's :threaded)"] [69 2 "// cimpl is whether the code is of the Python code that stands for CPython's C (cImplModules; trace.go's inCImpl,"] [70 2 "// queue 293): 0 not known yet, 1 not, 2 it is"] [76 1 "// codePos is an instruction's end line (less its line) and columns (0-based UTF-8 byte offsets), Col -1 when unknown:"] [77 1 "// co_positions' last three items (the first, the line, is Lines')."] [85 1 "// debugRanges is config.code_debug_ranges: false under -X no_debug_ranges or PYTHONNODEBUGRANGES (the code objects then"] [86 1 "// carry no columns: co_positions' None, no caret lines)"] [95 1 "// Position is instruction pc's location as co_positions gives it: line, end line, column, end column, each 0 when"] [96 1 "// unknown (ok false for the columns)."] [114 1 "// decodePositions reads positionsText: per instruction \"COL,END-COL[,END-LINE-LESS-LINE]\" or \"\" (no columns), \";\""] [115 1 "// between them (arbace.python.compile's positions-of). codePos.EndLine holds the end line less the line."] [141 1 "// compileWarning is a SyntaxWarning the compiler made: its message and location (1-based offsets, 0 unknown)."] [147 1 "// NativeFunc is a code object's compiled body (PY8's AOT, aot.go): it runs f from f.PC as step does"] [148 1 "// (the value returned, an error raised, or a *pushFrame for a call of a Python function)."] [151 1 "// CodeKind is the IR's :kind."] [166 1 "// CodeFlags are the IR's :flags."] [177 24 "// CO_ITERABLE_COROUTINE: a generator types.coroutine marked (set at run time, PY5d)"] [178 2 "// CodeFutureAnnotations and CodeFutureBarry: the source's (or the compile's inherited) from __future__ import"] [179 2 "// annotations and barry_as_FLUFL, co_flags' CO_FUTURE_ANNOTATIONS and CO_FUTURE_BARRY_AS_BDFL (py-os-1124)"] [184 1 "// coFutureMask are the future features compile() takes in its flags and a code's co_flags reports (PyCF_MASK's that"] [185 1 "// future.c sets: CO_FUTURE_BARRY_AS_BDFL, CO_FUTURE_ANNOTATIONS)."] [188 1 "// futureMode is a compile mode with the future features of flags (co_flags' bits) the compile inherits (py-os-1124): +futA"] [189 1 "// for annotations, +futB for barry_as_FLUFL (the host's compile-source binds the reader's and the compiler's features)."] [200 1 "// Instr is an instruction: the operation and its argument decoded into two integers (§7.2's table:"] [201 1 "// an index, a count, a jump target, an operator, a flag ...)."] [207 1 "// Handler is a row of the exception table: instructions [Start, End) go to Target with the stack"] [208 1 "// popped to Depth, then the instruction's index pushed when Lasti, then the exception."] [214 1 "// Make-function's parts (the IR's [CONST PARTS]), as a bit set in B."] [222 1 "// Intrinsic is the IR's :call-intrinsic NAME (§3.4)."] [243 1 "// codeTop is a code's own facts for the codes nested in it (queue 229, py-small-1127): its kind, instructions and names,"] [244 1 "// up the facts of the code whose constant it is (nil: the outermost), imports, on a module's, the names its scope binds by"] [245 1 "// import (made when asked)."] [254 1 "// topNode is c's own codeTop, made when absent."] [262 1 "// root is the outermost code's facts (c's own when c is no code's constant)."] [271 1 "// linkTops gives every code of the tree loaded at c its facts and each nested code's link to its parent's (ReadIR's, once"] [272 1 "// the tree is loaded: each code's instructions and names are final then)."] [284 1 "// Type makes a Code a node of the cycle collection (finalize.go's cyTraverse, py-small-1127): the code object's type;"] [285 1 "// a Code is never a Python value itself (Object gives its code object)."] [288 1 "// Object is c's code object, the same each time (f_code, __code__, gi_code: CPython's one PyCodeObject; queue 219t)."] [296 1 "// handlerAt is the handler covering instruction pc, or nil."] [307 1 "// Line is instruction pc's line, 0 when unknown (-1: none, in a replaced line table)."] [310 3 "// a replaced line table (queue 248): the view's line of the instruction's code unit, -1 for none"] [315 14 "// past the table's end"] [325 1 "// OpNames is the IR's operations the loader knows, in Op order (bin/pyi runtime check compares them"] [326 1 "// with arbace.python.ir/ops)."] [329 1 "// OpOwners is each operation's owner (PYI-SPEC.md §9), in Op order."] [332 1 "// SetFilename sets the code object's co_filename and its nested code objects'."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[107 26] [277 31] [309 16] [312 29] [336 31]] :go/trails [[240 75]]} (go/file "code.go" :imports [


